1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,480
There are five key metrics that determine whether a routine system will actually work for a busy woman like you.
有五个关键指标，可以用来判断一套日常安排是否真的适合像你这样忙碌的人。

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,240
Number one is time investment.
第一项是时间投入。

3
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,160
How much time the routine takes daily.
也就是这套安排每天需要多少时间。

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,840
Number two is startup overwhelm.
第二项是开始时的负担感。

5
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,400
How much of your life you have to adjust for the routine.
也就是为了这套安排，你得调整生活中的多少部分。

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:18,600
Number three is sustainability, which is basically how long you can realistically maintain this routine.
第三项是可持续性，简单说就是你实际上能把这个安排维持多久。

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,919
Number four is flexibility, which is what happens to this method when life gets messy.
第四项是灵活性，也就是生活一乱，这个方法还能怎样运作。

8
00:00:22,919 --> 00:00:25,549
And number five is realistic expectations.
第五项是切合实际的预期。

9
00:00:25,559 --> 00:00:28,279
Whether this routine actually fits into your lifestyle.
也就是这个安排究竟能不能融入你的生活方式。

10
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:31,150
So let's talk about method number one, the 5:00 a.m. club.
先说第一种方法：早上五点起床。

11
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,240
Time investment, 2 to 3 hours.
时间投入，两到三个小时。

12
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:39,400
Getting up at 5:00 a.m. requires you to wake up 2 to 3 hours earlier than you normally would, which is a lot.
五点起床意味着比平时早两到三个小时，这个变化可不小。

13
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:44,279
So if you're not used to waking up early or you're not a morning person, this is a huge adjustment.
所以，如果你不习惯早起，或者本来就不是早起型的人，这会是个很大的调整。

14
00:00:44,279 --> 00:00:46,199
Startup overwhelm is extreme.
刚开始时的负担感非常强。

15
00:00:46,199 --> 00:00:52,999
You have to literally change your sleep schedule, morning routine, and evening routine at the same time to accommodate waking up at 5:00 a.m.
你得同时调整睡觉时间、晨间安排和晚间安排，来适应五点起床。

16
00:00:52,999 --> 00:00:55,480
And I don't know about you, but that sounds terrible.
我不知道你怎么看，但这听起来可不轻松。

17
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:57,800
Sustainability is 2 to 3 weeks max.
能坚持的时间，最多两到三周。

18
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:04,760
I have never met anyone who's actually stuck with 5:00 a.m. wakeups longterm, unless they were already naturally early risers.
我没遇到过能长期坚持五点起床的人，除非他们原本就习惯自然早起。

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:10,829
Even when I was waking up at 5:00 a.m., I could only do it like 4 days out of the week, and my entire sleep schedule was messed up.
即使在我五点起床的那段时间，一周也只能做到大约四天，整个作息还被打乱了。

20
00:01:10,839 --> 00:01:14,279
Flexibility is zero, because what happens when you go to bed late?
灵活性是零，因为要是你睡晚了，会怎么样？

21
00:01:14,279 --> 00:01:17,320
You only get 3 hours of sleep and you feel like trash the next day.
你只睡了三个小时，第二天感觉糟透了。

22
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,559
So the entire system eventually just falls apart.
于是，整套安排最后就散掉了。

23
00:01:19,559 --> 00:01:23,160
And this is really only realistic for like 1% of the population.
这实际上可能只对百分之一的人可行。

24
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:27,960
So basically, this could work if you have no social life and can function on very little sleep.
所以简单说，如果没有社交活动、睡很少也能运转，这套方法也许才行。

25
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:30,440
Number two is the influencer morning routine.
第二种是博主式晨间日常。

26
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,360
Time investment is 1 to 3 hours.
时间投入是一到三个小时。

27
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:37,720
You're doing a 10-step skincare routine, a 60-minute Pilates class, 30 minutes of meditation, journaling.
你要做十步护肤、上六十分钟普拉提课、冥想三十分钟，还要写日记。

28
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,469
By the time you're done, it's noon, babe.
等你全部做完，都到中午了。

29
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:42,360
Let's be honest, this is only for people who don't work a 9 to5.
说实话，这只适合不用朝九晚五上班的人。

30
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,119
Startup overwhelm is high.
刚开始时的负担感很高。

31
00:01:44,119 --> 00:01:48,040
Trying to incorporate all of these is like adding 15 new habits at once.
要把这些都纳入日常，就像一下子增加十五个新习惯。

32
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,600
Sustainability, 1 month if you're lucky.
能坚持多久？运气好的话，一个月。

33
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:55,160
Like the 5 a.m. club, if you don't wake up early enough, you won't have time to do most of it.
和五点起床那套安排一样，如果起得不够早，多数项目就没时间做。

34
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,119
Plus, skincare and Pilates classes are expensive.
另外，护肤和普拉提课也不便宜。

35
00:01:58,119 --> 00:02:00,749
So if you don't got that influencer money, it's a no-go.
所以，如果没有博主那样的预算，这就行不通。

36
00:02:00,759 --> 00:02:02,280
Flexibility, medium.
灵活性，中等。

37
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:05,639
Again, it works great if you don't have to be at an office at 9:00 a.m.
还是那句话，如果不用早上九点到办公室，这种安排会比较好用。

38
00:02:05,639 --> 00:02:07,400
And realistic expectations.
再看预期是否切合实际。

39
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,000
This is an Instagram fantasy.
这是一种 Instagram 式的理想画面。

40
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,800
This routine method is purely designed for aesthetics.
这种日常方式完全是为了画面好看而设计的。

41
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,280
And method number three, using willpower.
第三种方法，靠意志力。

42
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:19,560
This takes constant mental energy because every decision you make requires some amount of willpower.
这会持续消耗心力，因为每个决定都需要一定的意志力。

43
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,720
The startup overwhelm is maximum.
刚开始时的负担感达到最高。

44
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:26,030
You're basically forcing yourself to do everything perfectly using pure determination.
你基本上是在单靠决心，逼自己把每件事都做得完美。

45
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,960
Sustainability is 2 weeks max.
能坚持的时间最多两周。

46
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,400
Willpower is finite.
意志力是有限的。

47
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,429
You will run out of it.
你会把它耗尽。

48
00:02:30,439 --> 00:02:32,280
Flexibility is basically negative.
灵活性基本是负数。

49
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:35,159
Any deviation will be clocked as weakness in your mind.
任何偏离计划的情况，都会被你视为自己不够坚定。

50
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:37,240
This is basically toxic productivity.
这基本就是有害的效率执念。

51
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:42,360
And this is all based on the myth that successful people just have more willpower, which is obviously not true.
这一切都建立在一个误解上：成功的人只是意志力更强；作者认为这显然不对。

52
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,920
Now, what would the perfect routine system look like?
那么，理想的日常安排会是什么样的呢？

53
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,319
I would want the time investment to be like 15 minutes.
我希望时间投入大约是十五分钟。

54
00:02:47,319 --> 00:02:49,319
It should fit into your existing schedule.
它应该能融入你已有的时间安排。

55
00:02:49,319 --> 00:02:51,319
The startup overwhelm should be minimal.
开始时的负担感应该尽可能小。

56
00:02:51,319 --> 00:02:54,840
You're able to make changes so gradually, your brain doesn't notice.
你可以很缓慢地做出改变，慢到自己都不太察觉。

57
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,000
This system should last a lifetime.
这套方法应该能长期用下去。

58
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,439
It should be built to last through real life, not just a season.
它应该经得起真实生活的变化，而不只是适用一小段时间。

59
00:03:00,439 --> 00:03:05,960
It also needs to have maximum flexibility so that it adapts with you even when life gets messy.
它还需要足够灵活，这样即使生活变乱，也能跟着你调整。

60
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:10,760
And again, it should be designed for real women with real lives, not just influencers.
再说一次，它应该为过着真实生活的人而设计，而不只是适合博主。
